WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.940
- Well, this is actually really cool,

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.330
'cause you're executive producing

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.270
and starring in the fifth
Chronical Mysteries.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.715
So what's it about for
people that don't know?

00:00:06.715 --> 00:00:07.760
(audience claps)

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:08.750
- Okay, so my character,

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.800
this is a franchise.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.810
Movies about, my character is a podcaster,

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.700
which just honestly comes
from my love of true crime,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.160
you know, the whole genre.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.150
And I really had to defend to my husband

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:23.350
why I spend so much time
listening to podcasts.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.365
And I was like, "Oh, I'm
working on a project here."

00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:26.230
(audience laughs)
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.400
So I developed a movie
series about my character is,

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.410
you know, follows these cold
cases, solves these crimes.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.810
And this is our fifth movie.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.230
It's been super fun.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.320
You just put up a photo.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.270
I actually got to, one
of the things I love

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.128
about being a producer is you
get to pull in your friends

00:00:41.128 --> 00:00:43.720
and pull on favors from your friends.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.970
And so Christian Alfonso, who
was on "Days of Our Lives"

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:47.640
for many years, a dear friend of mine,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:49.250
happened to be filming in Vancouver.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:53.080
And so I asked her to come play
the role for me in my movie.

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:54.610
And it just worked out.
- Wow.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.330
- She's an amazing dear friend.

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:58.520
Like because of the lock
downs and the quarantine,

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.800
everything, I literally wept in her arms

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.303
when I saw her on set for
the first time (laughs).

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.770
And so it's just been
an amazing experience.

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:10.390
And I love like taking that idea

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:13.070
of these armchair detectives
that we listened to.

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.400
I think I heard that you
liked true crime too.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.340
Is that right Kelly?

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:18.330
- Okay, here's the thing Allison.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.870
I used to be obsessed
with it, and I'd watch it,

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.050
and then I found myself being terrified.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:26.197
Like I was, I thought
watching it, I'd be like,

00:01:26.197 --> 00:01:27.880
"Oh I have all these ideas to like,

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.160
if someone comes in my window,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.420
then I'll do this.
(Allison laughs)

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:31.430
I gotta make sure to do this."

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:32.940
I thought I'd be, it'd be like, you know,

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:34.120
kind of empowering.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.110
No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:38.320
I ended up like literally
sleeping like with one eye open.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.270
I was just terrified
constantly all the time.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:41.540
So I had to stop.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:42.750
- So actually this case,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.860
the helped to depth story, did
come from my like fascination

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:48.970
with a bunch of true crime cases.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:50.710
You know, there's a lot about gurus

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.230
and some cult stuff that's happened lately

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.710
and like documentaries on Netflix

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.450
that I just like deep dive in.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:01:57.446
It's a rabbit hole.

00:01:57.446 --> 00:01:59.576
Netflix knows me so well, so.
- Yeah.

00:01:59.576 --> 00:02:00.409
(Kelly laughs)

